  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote the reef scene in `src/main.ts`. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser here, so none of it has been seen rendering. The layout, colours, fog density, light intensities and shader output are all unchecked guesses.\n\n- **Seabed:** a 90 m heightfield with rippled sand and per-vertex sand colour. An additive custom-shader overlay on the same mesh draws caustic light lines that drift over time.\n- **Water:** a teal gradient sky, a constant-colour fog (density 0.045) for the depth fade, a teal hemisphere light, and a shadow-casting sun from above. Nine additive god-ray planes hang in the water.\n- **Reef:** branching colonies, brain corals with ridged domes, lattice fan corals, tube clusters, table corals and rocks. All are instanced cylinders and spheres.\n- **Swaying life:** 70 segmented kelp strands and 5 anemones with 20 two-segment tentacles each. Both are re-posed every frame.\n- **Fish:** a loose school of 38 small fish (three colour groups) swimming along a shared wandering path. Three larger solitary fish (angelfish, parrotfish, grouper) follow their own elliptical orbits. Fish have a body, a wagging tail and a dorsal fin, and face their direction of travel.\n- **Bubbles and particles:** 48 bubbles rise from four vents, and 80 pale motes drift slowly.\n- **Camera:** it orbits at about 10.5 m, with a slight radius change, a height bob around 3 m, and a small target bob. It is driven each frame with `app.camera.setPose`. If that call has no effect, the camera will stay still, which is the main risk to check.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()`.\n- **Top-level await:** I avoided it by wrapping startup in an async function. I don't know the build target in use, and the default one may reject top-level await.\n\nIf the caustic or god-ray shader fails to compile, the engine skips those draws and logs `CUSTOM_SHADER_COMPILE_FAILED`. The rest of the scene would still draw.\n\n",
